<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        Stage gate (d), decision D1 = d-1 (2026-08-04 gate). CloseDate is platform-required
        and can never be blank, so an ISBLANK(CloseDate) reading of "Close Date set" would be
        a guaranteed no-op. Instead this blocks entry to About to Close when CloseDate is
        already in the PAST, forcing the deal-driver to re-set a realistic date before the
        deal enters the closing runway.

        errorDisplayField is CloseDate, not StageName, because CloseDate is the field the
        user must actually change and it is editable on the layout.

        Gate applies to the stage transition only (ISCHANGED); existing records already at
        About to Close are unaffected.
    -->
    <fullName>Close_Date_Before_About_To_Close</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks stage entry to About to Close when the Close Date is already in the past. See the XML comment in this file for full rationale.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(StageName),
    ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;About to Close&apos;),
    CloseDate &lt; TODAY()
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>CloseDate</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>Set a current Close Date before moving this deal to About to Close - the current Close Date is in the past.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
